act' and lists exactly 9 sites, none in composer.py / composer_edit.py.","src/rebar/_commands/composer.py:274 `cfg_root=os.path.dirname(str(tracker))` and :286 same; src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py:141 `cfg_root=os.path.dirname(str(tracker))`.","gates.py:319 `limit = int(compose_config(cfg_root).verify...)` and gates.py:323 `if not _plan_review_gate_applies(cfg_root, ...)` — cfg_root IS the config/gate root.","Plan scope note: 'This ticket carries the rest.' — but the composer cfg_root sites are not enumerated in 'the rest.'"],"finding":"The plan's inventory of dirname(tracker)-as-config-root sites omits three verified sites that pass os.path.dirname(str(tracker)) as cfg_root: composer.py:274 (description_cap_warning), composer.py:286 (duplicate_create_warning), and composer_edit.py:141 (description_cap_warning). cfg_root is fed to compose_config(cfg_root) to read config/gate flags (gates.py:113/319, recent_creates.py:156), and description_cap_warning routes cfg_root into _plan_review_gate_applies (gates.py:323) — the very plan-review gate the plan names as the regression. The str(tracker) wrapping means the plan's literal 'os.path.dirname(tracker)' enumeration and its guard AC miss them.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1e5d90c423a234be","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"## Sites (all verified present, `src/rebar`)","norm_id":"n854a09cf82e39f51","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["composer.py:274 / composer_edit.py:141: on a relocated store, description_cap_warning reads an empty config, so max_ticket_description_chars and the plan-review-gate-applies check silently misfire — the same OFF-reads-as-empty failure mode the plan proves for the gate flag.","composer.py:286: duplicate_create_warning reads compose_config(cfg_root).verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets from a directory with no rebar.toml, silently disabling duplicate-create suggestions on a relocated store.","The guard AC ('fails if a new os.path.